{{- /* internal/render/templates/finding.gohtml — one finding (§7.3): a
<details class="finding"> element whose id attribute is the qualified id,
verbatim, no substitution, in either qualifier form (§8.1), and whose
<summary> is headed by a derived headline — the first sentence of body,
truncated at a word boundary to a 140-rune cap — never the id. The id
survives as a small monospace chip beside the headline: still the anchor a
copied link resolves to, via fragmentHref (bead .2, html_href.go), and
still carrying the full qualified id in a title attribute. The profile is
its own tag, never folded into the headline or the chip; an
ordinal-qualified finding renders its own ordinal tag the same way. The
collapse default (open when Priority >= 7) is computed server-side into
htmlFindingView.Open (internal/render/html_view_finding.go) and rendered
here as the open attribute — never decided by script. Every finding
carries data-priority-css, data-category-css, and data-lens (§5.1),
each a grammar-constrained enum token, never a byte of reviewer prose.
Dot is htmlFindingView. */ -}}
{{define "finding"}}
<details class="finding" id="{{.ID}}" data-priority-css="{{.DataPriorityCSS}}" data-category-css="{{.DataCategoryCSS}}" data-lens="{{.DataLens}}"{{if .Open}} open{{end}}>
<summary>
<span class="finding-headline">{{.Headline}}</span>
<a class="finding-id" href="#{{fragmentHref .ID}}" title="{{.ID}}">{{.ChipText}}</a>
{{if .HasProfile}}<span class="tag tag-profile">{{.Profile}}</span>{{end}}
{{if .HasOrdinal}}<span class="tag tag-ordinal">{{.OrdinalTag}}</span>{{end}}
<span class="tag {{.DataPriorityCSS}}">priority {{.Priority}}</span>
<span class="tag {{.DataCategoryCSS}}">{{.Category}}</span>
</summary>
<div class="finding-body">
<p class="anchors">{{if .Anchors}}{{range .Anchors}}<code class="tag anchor">{{.}}</code>{{end}}{{else}}(none){{end}}</p>
<p class="body">{{.Body}}</p>
{{if .HasCode}}{{template "code" .Code}}{{end}}
{{if .Suggestions}}{{template "suggestion" .Suggestions}}{{end}}
</div>
</details>
{{end}}
